meta {
  name: 64 PT Categories
  seq: 64
}

docs {
  # PT (Patient) Categories

  Registration › Registration Settings › **PT Category** — a per-branch pricing
  category that maps to a **Lab Test List** + **Lab Panel List**
  (`BranchLabTestList` / `BranchLabPanelList`), identical to how referrals map to
  lists. Unlike Patient Categories (tenant-level, multi-mapping), a PT category is
  **tenant-scoped + branch-level**: it belongs to the caller's active branch
  (from the JWT profile — requires a business token with an active branch set,
  else `ACTIVE_BRANCH_REQUIRED`).

  - A **"General"** default (unmapped, active) is auto-created **per branch** on
    branch creation (`branch.created` event) — no separate seed request. Being
    unmapped, GENERAL never participates in pricing (it's a default selection
    only) and is pre-selected on the Create-Order page.
  - At least one of `branchLabTestListId` / `branchLabPanelListId` is required on
    create (`PT_CATEGORY_MAPPING_REQUIRED`); the ids must exist in the caller's
    branch (`INVALID_PT_CATEGORY_LAB_TEST_LIST` / `..._LAB_PANEL_LIST`).
  - `categoryName` is unique per branch among active rows
    (`PT_CATEGORY_NAME_CONFLICT`).
  - Only one category can be the branch's default at a time — setting a new
    default clears the previous one. `GET /pt-categories/default` returns it.
  - Categories cannot be deleted (no DELETE route) — only deactivated — to
    preserve historical order pricing. Inactive categories are excluded from the
    Create-Order options feed.

  **Pricing integration.** During Create Order, `GET /referral-lists/resolve`
  accepts `ptCategoryId` and folds it into the pricing chain at priority slot 2:
  **B2B Panel → PT Category → Referred-by Doctor → Internal → External →
  Walk-in**. A selected PT category resolves to its mapped Lab Test List / Lab
  Panel List directly; an unmapped category (e.g. GENERAL) is skipped and the
  resolver falls through to the next priority.

  All routes are business-authenticated (`Bearer {{businessAccessToken}}`);
  tenant comes from the JWT, active branch from the JWT profile. Writes are
  audited under `AuditModule.PT_CATEGORY`.
}
